# Build-context exclusions.
#
# SECURITY: anything not excluded here is baked into an immutable image layer by
# `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile. Secrets in the build context are recoverable by
# anyone who can pull the image or `docker history` it -- deleting the file in a
# later layer does NOT remove it. Keep this list ahead of new tooling configs.

# Runtime data / build artefacts
zipper
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
.git
.gitignore

# Secrets and credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.session
*.session-journal
# NOTE: admin.txt is deliberately NOT excluded -- tools.get_admin_ids() reads it
# at runtime and an absent file silently disables every admin command. It is
# already public in git, so excluding it buys no confidentiality. The real fix
# is to move the admin list into validated env config (audit finding Z-18);
# exclude it here only once that lands.

# Local tooling configs (may embed API keys)
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Dev-only files that need not ship in the runtime image
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.python-version
README.md
LICENSE
app.json
docker-compose.yml
tests
pytest.ini
